.TH SSH-KEYGEN 1
.SH NAME
ssh-keygen \- make a new SSH key pair
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssh-keygen
.RB [ \-t
.BR ed25519 ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-C
.IR comment ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ssh-keygen
makes a new Ed25519 key pair in OpenSSH's file format (unencrypted): the
private key in
.I ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
(or
.IR file )
and the public key, one line, in the same name with
.B .pub
added, which it also prints. Copy that line into the server's
.I ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
to log in there with the key. An existing key is never overwritten.
.PP
.B ssh-keygen
is another name of
.BR ssh (1)
.RI ( /bin/ssh-keygen
is a link to it).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t ed25519
The key type; Ed25519 is the only one.
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
Where to write the private key.
.TP
.BI \-C " comment"
The public key's comment
.RI ( user @ host
by default).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0; 255 if the file exists or cannot be written; 1 for a usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 \fRand\fP ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
The key pair.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR sshd (8)
.SH BUGS
Ed25519 only; no passphrase.
